Author: James Cherti &#60;https://www.jamescherti.com/&#62; License: GPL The proxymacs Emacs package simplifies HTTP, HTTPS, and SOCKS proxy configuration. It supports HTTP/HTTPS proxies and SOCKS4, SOCKS4a, and SOCKS5. Usage HTTP and HTTPS Proxy (setq proxymacs-proxy-type 'http) (setq proxymacs-http-host &#34;127.0.0.1&#34;) (setq proxymacs-http-port 3128) ; accepts integer or string (setq proxymacs-http-no-proxy &#34;^\\(localhost\\&#124;127\\.0\\.0\\.1\\&#124;10\\..*\\&#124;192\\.168\\..*\\)&#34;) ;; Optional HTTPS configuration (falls back to HTTP host and port when nil): ;; (setq proxymacs-https-host &#34;127.0.0.1&#34;) ;; (setq proxymacs-https-port 3128) ;; Optional HTTP authentication: ;; (setq proxymacs-http-realm &#34;Proxy&#34;) ;; (setq proxymacs-http-user &#34;my_user&#34;) ;; (setq proxymacs-http-password &#34;my_password&#34;) ;; Optional HTTPS authentication (falls back to HTTP authentication when nil): ;; (setq proxymacs-https-realm &#34;Proxy&#34;) &#8230; <a href="https://www.jamescherti.com/proxymacs-el/">Continue reading <span class="meta-nav">&#8594;</span></a>